  "claimBoundary": [
    "success conformance is exact for static grayscale16, grayscale+alpha16, RGB16 and RGBA16 PNG with explicit color authority and full-resolution output in non-interlaced or Adam7 form; all four source models qualify explicit sRGB, RGB16/RGBA16 additionally qualify preserve-source embedded RGB ICC, and RGB16/RGBA16 qualify exact raw full-range cICP signaling for Display-P3 SDR, BT.2100 PQ and BT.2100 HLG; convert-to-sRGB has an in-gamut cICP Display-P3 12/13/0/1 slice and a generic monitor/input-class RGB/XYZ matrix/TRC ICC slice with no sBIT/HDR metadata or gamut mapping: class-only paired cases hold stored source, matrix/TRC tags and profile size fixed while changing `mntr` to `scnr`, and require identical canonical pixels plus identical operation/transfer bounds; output-class `prtr` remains fail-closed; two unmodified ICC Profile Library scene-referred `scnr` profiles are retained as real-profile negatives and must fail at the LUT/MPE semantic gate despite an enlarged metadata budget, proving that input-class admission does not imply generic input-profile admission; two success cases additionally retain one 724-byte `scnr` gamma+matrix research profile derived from a real Epson 3170 no-color-correction 48-bit scan and 288 measured IT8 patches, in linear and Adam7 scan order, with exact fixture/tool/source provenance and without claiming it is a vendor profile; every ICC source requires a nondegenerate authored colorant matrix and no LUT/MPE transform; monitor-class `mntr` additionally requires D50 media white within fixed-point quantization tolerance and a matrix that reconstructs that white, while input-class `scnr` treats `wtpt` as captured-medium metadata and requires nonnegative X/Z plus positive Y without requiring device code white to equal D50; and either one shared qualified RGB TRC—parametric type-0 through type-4 whose admitted source-domain mapping is finite, normalized, weakly nondecreasing and requires no source-value clipping, or curveType count=0