    "the deterministic generator retains the stored 16-bit source bytes independently; classic libpng reads or expands them to straight RGBA16 without strip16 or byte swapping, and that external RGBA16 big-endian value must equal an independently constructed expected value; for ICC success cases the generator also retains deterministic profile bytes and libpng png_get_iCCP must return those bytes exactly, cICP success cases require libpng png_get_cICP to return the generator's four signaling bytes exactly, and PQ static-HDR cases require png_get_mDCV_fixed/png_get_cLLI_fixed to reproduce the stored integer metadata exactly before any pixel transform; cICP Display-P3 conversion uses a separate W3C CSS Color 4 P3-to-XYZ then XYZ-to-linear-sRGB rational-matrix oracle, while every qualified ICC matrix/TRC conversion independently parses that profile's own s15Fixed16 XYZ colorants and all three channel TRC encodings, applies either the exact parametric type-0 through type-4 equation (including type-1/type-2 threshold semantics and type-4 e/f offsets), curveType count=0 identity, curveType count=1 `Y=X^gamma` with gamma decoded from the stored u8Fixed8 value, or normalized weakly-nondecreasing count>1 samples with uniform-domain linear interpolation; it rejects profiles whose admitted source mapping would require clipping plus sampled tables with non-zero start/non-65535 end or decreasing entries, then targets the ICC reference sRGB D50 matrix, requires exact deterministic UInt16 output; LittleCMS 2.x relative-colorimetric 16-bit output remains an independent implementation observation with alpha unchanged, retaining the historical <=1-code regression gate for previously qualified shared/per-channel-type0 and 5-node sampled cases while mixed per-channel parametric, mixed-encoding, 1025-node large-sampled and real-measurement-derived input cases require successful CMS execution and record the observed RGB delta without promoting that delta into a normative whole-domain tolerance; the retained real Epson-derived fixture currently observes a maximum 16-code RGB difference on its measured in-gamut samples while exact profile-tag math remains the normative oracle",
    "ImageCraft output is a separate codec-owned straight RGBA16 value with canonical little-endian samples; preserve-source capture independently converts the expected RGBA16 big-endian oracle to little-endian and requires exact equality, while every convert-to-sRGB success requires exact equality to its independent transformed 16-bit oracle with alpha unchanged; preserve-source embedded RGB ICC bytes are retained as value color authority and charged in transferred output, while converted ICC output publishes sRGB and drops the profile from the transferred representation but keeps sourceColorProfile=embeddedICC as provenance; changing qualified ICC matrix/TRC tags, TRC encoding kind or parametric function number changes the exact output even when source pixels are identical, which is explicitly covered by the non-P3 parametric type-0/type-1/type-2/type-3/type-4 and curveType identity/gamma/sampled cases; preserve-source cICP is retained as fixed structured authority with zero payload charge and sourceColorProfile remains unknown, while converted cICP P3 output publishes sRGB with sourceColorProfile still unknown; PQ mDCV/cLLI remain separate fixed integer HDR metadata rather than being folded into color encoding or interpreted as a tone-map policy",
